From 4ed1590a291dd4b311a4e18f0de20526712c7173 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Furruka <3483930638@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:59:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] eccci: write the CCIF SRAM info tail to the MD window as well

ccci_reset_ccif_hw() zeroes BOTH CCIF SRAM views and then republishes the
"smem info" tail - magic 0x7274626E, the MDSS_DBG region's MD-view address and
its size, i.e. the coordinates the modem reads early in its boot - to baseA
only. The vendor code can afford that because on stock LK pre-writes the MD
side; here the clear loop wipes it and nothing puts it back, so the modem's own
view stays all zero, it stalls at early boot and never sends HS1.

That is not a guess: this device's boot status is exactly 0x5443000C /
0x53320000 ("TC" / "S2"), and the MT6895-Mainline pearl port reports the same
stall (boot_status TC/S2, never sends HS1) fixed by exactly these three writes
to baseB, verified there as reaching HS1 plus the 46-feature negotiation.

baseB is the same MD CCIF window the clear loop above already writes, so this
adds no new access class.

(cherry picked from commit 60e35be508f38c136d0180799cfb90cbdcf6f95e)
Link: https://github.com/MT6895-Mainline/linux/commit/60e35be508f38c136d0180799cfb90cbdcf6f95e (qqcandy branch)
[dianqk: applied to the MT6897 vendor copy with reduced context (its
 export line differs); no code change]
Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_ccif.c   | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_ccif.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_ccif.c
index bae94bfba3..79b5d42b3c 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_ccif.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_ccif.c
@@ -1142,6 +1142,25 @@ void ccci_reset_ccif_hw(int ccif_id, void __iomem *baseA,
 	ccif_write32(baseA,
 		PCCIF_CHDATA + PCCIF_SRAM_SIZE - sizeof(u32),
 		region->size);
+	/*
+	 * qqcandy: the tail above goes to the AP-side view only, and the vendor
+	 * code can afford that because on stock LK pre-writes the MD side. Our
+	 * clear loop above zeroes BOTH views, so without these writes the MD's
+	 * own view stays all zero, the modem stalls at early boot (boot_status
+	 * 0x5443000C/0x53320000 = "TC"/"S2") and never sends HS1 - exactly what
+	 * this device shows. Same three values, written to the MD window.
+	 * (Cross-checked against the MT6895-Mainline pearl port, whose comment
+	 * and verified result report the same stall and the same fix.)
+	 */
+	ccif_write32(baseB,
+		PCCIF_CHDATA + PCCIF_SRAM_SIZE - 3 * sizeof(u32),
+		0x7274626E);
+	ccif_write32(baseB,
+		PCCIF_CHDATA + PCCIF_SRAM_SIZE - 2 * sizeof(u32),
+		region->base_md_view_phy);
+	ccif_write32(baseB,
+		PCCIF_CHDATA + PCCIF_SRAM_SIZE - sizeof(u32),
+		region->size);
 }
 //EXPORT_SYMBOL(ccci_reset_ccif_hw);
 
